      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Intermittent interface errors can indeed be a physical layer issue, but there are many other possibilities as well. EMI (electromagnetic interference) from nearby devices, nearby physical infrastructure reconfigurations, or even cables themselves are common culprits. Additionally, hardware issues such as faulty Ethernet ports, driver bugs, or operating system issues could also be causing this erratic behavior. You may want to try physical troubleshooting by swapping out cables or checking the network interface card (NIC) configuration to isolate the issue.",
